# 4 Experimental Setup

We consider 13 datasets<sup>5</sup> with varying imbalance levels. Table 1 shows the datasets along with the total number of documents belonging to the majority and minority classes, dataset identifier, and imbalance ratio (IR), defined as (Orriols-Puig and Bernadó-Mansilla, 2009), $IR = \frac{\text{class majority}}{\text{class minority}}$ - the higher the IR, the more imbalanced the dataset. All adopted datasets have two classes, as this work focuses on binary classification problems.

